    'A company is considering issuing new debentures with a face value of ₹1,000, paying an annual interest of ₹80. The debentures are expected to be issued at par (₹1,000). The corporate tax rate is 30%. What is the approximate after-tax cost of debt?',
    '["5.60%","8.00%","8.42%","12.00%"]'::jsonb,
    0,
    'The before-tax cost of debt is calculated as the annual interest payment divided by the net proceeds. Here, Annual Interest = ₹80 and Net Proceeds = ₹1,000. So, Before-tax cost = 80 / 1000 = 0.08 or 8%. The after-tax cost of debt is calculated as: Before-tax cost * (1 - Tax Rate). After-tax cost = 8% * (1 - 0.30) = 8% * 0.70 = 5.60%.',
